> Seems correct; I assume ShadowRealm globals are not EventTargets.

[This is something I mentioned](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-shadowrealm/issues/324#issuecomment-1076983369) in the thread linked by @mhofman, but in practice the only additional thing SES would have to do if `globalThis` was an `EventTarget` is just to perform `Object.setPrototypeOf(globalThis, Object.prototype)` (and presumably they have to do something similar already to scrub `<iframe>`-based globals today).

The main restriction that would need to imposed is just that the prototype must be mutable on the `globalThis` object so that these APIs can be removed easily if they're not on the whitelist. (This is not the case with `window` today, I think existing SES-like implementations just strip all properties off `EventTarget` so it no longer has any functionality).

Another alternative entirely could just be to just hang some event target off `globalThis` for accessing things like promise rejection handlers:

```js
globalThis.events.addEventListener("unhandledrejection", () => {
    // ...whatever you're doing here
});
```

Although this would require some spec changes to define these objects and make sure the targets are correct in any specs that reference them.
